KNOWNBUG
s_eventually5.sv
--bound 2
^\[main\.p0\] always \(s_eventually \[3:3\] main\.c == 3\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.p1\] always \(s_eventually \[2:3\] main\.c == 3\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.p2\] always \(s_nexttime\[3\] main\.c == 3\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
property_obligations_rec (src/trans-word-level/property.cpp) truncates
the range of sva_ranged_s_eventually at the last time frame, and then
requires the operand to hold in the truncated range.  When the range
extends beyond the bound, the truncated disjunction can be false even
though the operand may hold in a time frame that is not in the
unwinding.  EBMC reports REFUTED for p0 and p1.  The same defect also
affects "s_eventually [a:b] p" used as an assumption, where the truncated
range makes the assumption stronger than intended.
